  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: not between R. Sadjour and R. Khabour.</p>\r\n<p>NB: There is an uncited reference <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.geonames.org/11886746/thapsacus.html\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">in Geonames</a> connecting the ruins at <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../481573620\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Jebel Khalid</a> to Thapsacus that seems to reflect older scholarship rejected e.g., by <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/2533/items/D6GEBUZB\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Gawlikowski 1996</a>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The location of the ancient site of Thapsacus is no longer known, but it lay on the western bank of the Euphrates River.",
